=== SURVEY ===
Web source MetricSwitcherChart.tsx = a presentational chart with a pill row above it for switching the
displayed metric (overview surfaces where one chart answers several questions). Generic over
`P extends {date}`; props: title, ariaLabel, series (Record<key,[P]>), metrics[{key,label,chart('bar'|
'area'|'line'),color,accent,unit,getValue,formatValue,formatTick}], activeMetric, onMetricChange,
height(=220), formatXTick, emptyMessage, action, testId. Body:
  • active = metrics.find(key===activeMetric) ?? metrics[0]
  • data  = series[active.key] ?? [] ; project P → {date, __value} via getValue (default p.value)
  • render branch: projected.length === 0 → <EmptyState message={emptyMessage}/> ; else a Recharts
    BarChart / AreaChart / LineChart per active.chart, with formatValue on the tooltip, formatTick ??
    formatValue on the Y-axis, and formatXTick on the X-axis.
  • the pill row (<PillFilterBar>) lives in the ChartContainer title-bar action area — always rendered.
Data sources (P1/S8): none — it is purely presentational (the parent owns the fetch); its only hook is
useTranslation (P1/S10). Shared components: forms/PillFilterBar, feedback/EmptyState. Charts: Recharts
Bar/Area/Line. Canonical native peers studied: shared-surfaces/AnnotationList (the props-driven leaf +
P4 loading/error/stale/offline freshness contract) and shared-surfaces/ChartExportMenu (the
chart-component leaf + telemetry/strings seams); the atomic chart primitives in
Sources/Components/Charts (TSBarChart/TSAreaChart/TSLineChart/TSChartContainer/TSChartPalette) and the
pill bar TSPillFilterBar / TSEmptyState.

=== REASONING ===
- The native surface composes Swift Charts DIRECTLY (BarMark / AreaMark+LineMark / LineMark over a
  categorical date X-axis) exactly as the web composes Recharts primitives directly — not via a generic
  wrapper — because the web component hand-picks per-metric chart kinds + custom axis/tooltip
  formatters that no single wrapper exposes. Token-styled grid + axis labels (Color.TS/Font.TS), a
  drag-to-inspect RuleMark tooltip (the HIG-native parity of the web hover <Tooltip>), and the metric's
  tick formatter on the Y-axis. Map: web Recharts → Swift Charts (done); web Leaflet → MapKit (n/a).
- The pill switcher is the native parity of web PillFilterBar — it mirrors TSPillFilterBar's capsule
  styling / accent-selected fill / horizontal scroll / .isSelected trait while rendering the
  facade-resolved labels verbatim (the shared TSPillFilterBar takes a LocalizedStringKey, which cannot
  carry our custom-table + verbatim/dynamic labels — so the surface mirrors its contract for
  Text(verbatim:) labels). A non-matching activeMetric key highlights nothing while the chart falls
  back to metrics[0] — the faithful web `find ?? metrics[0]` + non-matching PillItem behaviour.
- Architecture mirrors the AnnotationList props-driven leaf (.Source value types + .Projection pure
  projection + .Model state-holder/telemetry/i18n + .swift View + .Views subviews + .Previews):
  • Source (Foundation): MetricSwitcherChartKind (bar/area/line), MetricSwitcherValueFormat (web
    formatValue/formatTick — plain/integer/decimal/suffixed, non-finite → em dash), MetricSwitcherText
    (caller-localised key+fallback / verbatim), MetricSwitcherMetricSpec, MetricSwitcherPoint
    (projected {date,value}), MetricSwitcherDataset, MetricSwitcherConnection, MetricSwitcherChartLayout
    (height=220), MetricSwitcherChartLogic (activeMetric resolution, non-finite sanitiser, axis-label
    thinning ≈ preserveStartEnd, a11y summary).
  • Projection (Foundation): MetricSwitcherInput + .from(LoadableState) "cached → projection" adapter,
    MetricSwitcherResolved (Body: loading/error/empty/chart + pills + freshness + height),
    MetricSwitcherProjection (web chart/empty branch + P4 freshness). Localisation applied here.
  • Model (Foundation/Observation/OSLog): MetricSwitcherChartMeta (slug "MetricSwitcherChart"),
    MetricSwitcherChartTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default + Diagnostics seam,
    MetricSwitcherChartStrings (P1/S10 facade), @MainActor @Observable MetricSwitcherChartModel (owns
    the controlled selection + dataset state + optional retry; select()/retry()/update();
    markAppeared() emits view.opened once).
  • swift (the View): the panel bound through the model; designated + loaded-data + full-LoadableState
    inits. Views: panel chrome / pill bar / Swift Charts canvas / empty / loading / error / freshness
    chip. Previews: bar / area / line / interactive / empty / loading / error / stale / offline.
  • strings: the surface-owned keys (empty/error/loading/freshness/a11y summary). Tests + ModelTests.
- States: the web source for THIS surface has the chart branch + the empty branch (+ the
  non-matching-key fallback) — reproduced faithfully. Because it is a data-displaying surface whose
  parent owns the fetch, the P4 leaf contract (loading skeleton / error+retry / stale chip / offline
  cached+chip) is layered on the P1/S8 LoadableState the parent feeds — every one renders (no hidden
  surface), driven by the pure .from(LoadableState) adapter + projection.
- Side effects off the view: the @MainActor @Observable model owns the selection mutation + the
  view.opened emission; no HTTP and no Task plumbing in the view (Swift 6 strict concurrency).
- Rejected: porting Tailwind classes / raw hex (used P1/S9 tokens); a numeric X-axis (web uses
  type="category" date labels → categorical Swift Charts axis); hiding the surface when empty (web
  renders <EmptyState> + keeps the pill row → reproduced; never a blank box).

